{#
  The polling wrapper around the patient queue table.

  Rendered in BOTH places that show the table — inline from new.html.twig on
  first load, and on its own from the rows endpoint on every poll — so the
  server-rendered markup and the refreshed markup are byte-for-byte the same
  template. There is no "initial version" and "updated version" to drift apart.

  Expects everything _patient_rows.html.twig expects, plus `trial`.

  ── target="_top" is doing real work here ────────────────────────────────────
  By default every link and form inside a <turbo-frame> navigates *within* that
  frame. That would be wrong twice over: the Queue form's redirect carries flash
  messages that live outside the frame (so the confirmation would silently
  vanish), and the "view evaluation" links would try to render a whole detail
  page inside a table cell. target="_top" makes all navigation originating in
  here drive the full page, exactly as it did before Turbo was involved.

  Only the poller's programmatic reload() updates the frame — which is precisely
  the split we want: user actions behave identically with and without
  JavaScript, and the enhancement is confined to refreshing statuses.
#}
<turbo-frame id="evaluation-rows"
             target="_top"
             data-controller="evaluation-poll"
             data-evaluation-poll-url-value="{{ path('lumina_ui_evaluation_new_rows', {trial: trial.id}) }}"
             data-evaluation-poll-interval-value="5000">
  {% include '@LuminaUi/evaluation/_patient_rows.html.twig' %}
</turbo-frame>
